{"name":"Private Tone","hex":"#845469","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"private","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging or pertaining to an individual person, group of people, or entity that is not the state.","Relating to an individual or group of individuals outside of their official roles; often, sensitive or personal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A soldier of the lowest rank in the army.","A doctor working in privately rather than publicly funded health care."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/private"},{"term":"tone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A specific pitch.","(in the diatonic scale) An interval of a major second."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to give a particular tone to","to change the colour of"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"private":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-private.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/81/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-private.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Perseph